{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["Therefore 'and Elohim led the people about by the way of the wilderness' — a distant land, as it is written: ״אחד עשר יום מחורב״ and so on. But the Philistines alone intervened between Egypt and the land of Canaan. As is proven in the case of Isaac, who was going down from the land of Canaan to travel through the land of the Philistines to the land of Egypt because of the famine, until the Holy One, blessed be He, said to him: ״גור בארץ הזאת״. And Isaac dwelt in Gerar." "'And armed' — with weapons, for they were going to take possession of the land of Canaan, as it is written above: ״ואומר אעלה אתכם מעני מצרים אל ארץ הכנעני״ and so on. And likewise: ״תעברו חמושים״ of Joshua."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 13, :notes {0 "The lemma and proof texts are unaddressed in the source; addresses are Genesis 26:2–6 and Deuteronomy 1:2 respectively.", 1 "The first proof text is Exodus 3:17, the second Joshua 1:14; both are unaddressed in the source."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:41:25.259165009Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}